# Drafted by Gemini (R19 rites), edited. The five Final Rites of Maidenmist; logic by hand.


~ crimson_start
if flag.mm_crimson_guardians_dead
-> crimson_honor
endif
Narrator: Cold soot clings to the iron brazier among the marble tombs of the Highborn Crypts. Only the pale ring of the hound's lantern keeps the clammy grave fog from swallowing your boots.
yorgrim [weary]: Sir Marius Renathyr served a god of the morning and loved his sworn liege, King Viktor Denathria, like a brother. He rode a white charger named Dawn to hunt down every wicked thing on the road. Only the priestess Lethica could ever cool the terrible heat of his wrath.
* [if item:mm_dried_rose] Place the kindling in the brazier -> crimson_kindle
* I have no kindling yet -> crimson_nokindle
* Tell us again what you know of Marius -> crimson_start
* We will be back -> END

~ crimson_nokindle
yorgrim [neutral]: The kindling lies hidden near the tombs, though the fog has eaten the place from my mind. Search the stones again, for nothing is lost yet.
-> END

~ crimson_kindle
take mm_dried_rose
set mm_crimson_kindled
Narrator: Dry tinder catches with a sharp hiss, and a hungry crimson flame climbs the rusted bowl. The grave mist curdles thick around the pillars as ancient crypt guardians claw free of the marble to feed the fire.
yorgrim [angry]: Hold your ground inside the lantern light and strike down every waking bone. Their husks must fall where the fire can see them die.
combat mm_crimson_rite

~ crimson_honor
if not flag.mm_crimson_began
set mm_crimson_began
set mm_crimson_round = 0
set mm_crimson_succ = 0
set mm_crimson_bright = 0
endif
-> crimson_rite

~ crimson_rite
if flag.mm_crimson_succ >= 6
-> crimson_done
endif
if flag.mm_yorgrim_spent and flag.mm_crimson_succ >= 4
-> crimson_done
endif
if flag.mm_crimson_round >= 10
-> crimson_dies
endif
Narrator: The crimson fire wavers in the cold draft, waiting for you to feed it true words of the knight's road, his royal oath, or the woman who gentled his heart.
* Tell of the rides and the fights -> crimson_a
* Speak the oath he kept -> crimson_b
* Speak of the one who calmed him -> crimson_c
* Step back from the flame for now -> END


~ crimson_a
if flag.mem_marius_feats
advantage checks next: you remember Marius
endif
Narrator: You turn your voices toward the long roads Marius rode and the monsters he broke beneath Dawn's hooves. Each of you searches for the right words to honor his tireless blade.
* [Athletics DC 15] Tell of the rides and the fights, the way you have heard it -> crimson_a_ok | crimson_a_miss
* [Acrobatics DC 15] Tell of the rides and the fights, another way -> crimson_a_ok | crimson_a_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> crimson_a_ok | crimson_a_miss
* Choose another theme -> crimson_rite

~ crimson_a_ok
set mm_crimson_succ += 1
set mm_crimson_round += 1
if flag.mem_marius_feats
set mm_crimson_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The crimson fire leaps high with a sound like ringing steel and galloping hooves. Your words strike true, warming the cold marble with the memory of his valor on the road.
-> crimson_rite

~ crimson_a_miss
set mm_crimson_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: Your words ring hollow against the crypt stones, and the flame twists into a cruel puppet of a butcher trampling the weak under iron hooves. Every soul within the lantern circle flinches at the bitter laughter hissing from the mist.
-> crimson_rite


~ crimson_b
if flag.mem_marius_oath
advantage checks next: you remember Marius
endif
Narrator: You speak now of his morning god and the brotherhood he swore to King Viktor Denathria. Each hero reaches for words worthy of an unbreakable oath.
* [History DC 15] Speak the oath he kept, the way you have heard it -> crimson_b_ok | crimson_b_miss
* [Religion DC 15] Speak the oath he kept, another way -> crimson_b_ok | crimson_b_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> crimson_b_ok | crimson_b_miss
* Choose another theme -> crimson_rite

~ crimson_b_ok
set mm_crimson_succ += 1
set mm_crimson_round += 1
if flag.mem_marius_oath
set mm_crimson_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: A clean golden heat swells inside the crimson flame as your tribute lands true. The fire remembers the morning light and the king he loved as blood.
-> crimson_rite

~ crimson_b_miss
set mm_crimson_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: The tribute falters, and the spiteful dead twist the fire into the shape of a kneeling dog choking on a broken crown. A cold shudder runs through the party as the fog jeers at his ruined vow.
-> crimson_rite


~ crimson_c
if flag.mem_marius_love
advantage checks next: you remember Marius
endif
Narrator: You turn the rite toward the quiet priestess who alone could still the storm in his blood. Each of you reaches for a gentle truth to lay upon the coals.
* [Investigation DC 15] Speak of the one who calmed him, the way you have heard it -> crimson_c_ok | crimson_c_miss
* [Perception DC 15] Speak of the one who calmed him, another way -> crimson_c_ok | crimson_c_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> crimson_c_ok | crimson_c_miss
* Choose another theme -> crimson_rite

~ crimson_c_ok
set mm_crimson_succ += 1
set mm_crimson_round += 1
if flag.mem_marius_love
set mm_crimson_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The jagged crimson tongues soften and rise steady and bright at the sound of your words. Even the bitter ash smells briefly of night-blooming herbs and quiet peace.
-> crimson_rite

~ crimson_c_miss
set mm_crimson_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: The words stumble, and the shrouded spirits contort the flame into a weeping figure turning her back on a raving brute. Everyone who hears the wet, mocking sob from the brazier flinches back.
-> crimson_rite


~ crimson_dies
Narrator: The last grain of time runs out and the crimson fire gutters into cold black smoke. Yorgrim presses his spectral hand to the iron bowl, tearing a pale silver splinter from his own spirit to keep a single ember alive.
set mm_soul_fragments += 1
set mm_rite_fails += 1
disadvantage checks 1h: a piece of your soul is in the fire
set mm_crimson_round = 0
set mm_crimson_succ = 0
set mm_crimson_bright = 0
if flag.mm_rite_fails >= 2
set mm_yorgrim_spent
yorgrim [weary]: I will feed more of my own marrow into the ash so fewer words are needed next time. My chains feel heavier now, and the stones are growing dim.
else
yorgrim [neutral]: Gather your breath and try the rite once more, for no blame rests on your tongues.
endif
-> END

~ crimson_done
set beacon_crimson = 1
if flag.mm_crimson_bright >= 3
set beacon_crimson = 2
endif
if flag.mm_crimson_bright >= 6
set beacon_crimson = 3
endif
set mm_beacons_lit += 1
set mm_crimson_done
cutscene mm_beacon_lit
Narrator: The crimson beacon roars skyward in a pillar of hot blood-red light, driving the clammy shroud back from the Highborn Crypts. Far across the cemetery grounds, a single iron sconce catches fire high above the sepulcher doors.
yorgrim [smile]: You have given Marius back his morning light and his clean blade. Rest well, old friend, until the dawn returns.
if flag.mm_beacons_lit >= 5
set sepulcher_open
if not quest.maidenmist_dead_rise >= sepulcher
quest maidenmist_dead_rise sepulcher
endif
yorgrim [weary]: Five fires burn alongside my cold azure flame, and the heavy locks on the sepulcher doors have finally given way. Come back to the center, for our work lies below.
endif
-> END


~ violet_start
if flag.mm_violet_guardians_dead
-> violet_honor
endif
Narrator: Wet bone-ash crunches underfoot around the cold iron brazier of the Cremation Gardens. Only the steady glow of the hound's lantern holds the pressing wall of mist at bay.
yorgrim [weary]: Lethica Nightborne wore the barn owl symbol of the Nightmother, goddess of night, healing, and motherhood. Sick pilgrims walked miles for her cures, though she hid her face behind a quiet mask until love found her. She alone could quiet Marius's fierce anger, and she gave him her whole heart in return.
* [if item:mm_owl_feather] Place the kindling in the brazier -> violet_kindle
* I have no kindling yet -> violet_nokindle
* Tell us again what you know of Lethica -> violet_start
* We will be back -> END

~ violet_nokindle
yorgrim [neutral]: The kindling is tucked somewhere among the urns, though my worn memory cannot hold the spot. Look again through the ash, for nothing is lost.
-> END

~ violet_kindle
take mm_owl_feather
set mm_violet_kindled
Narrator: A spark takes hold in the damp tinder, sending a tall violet flame curling up from the iron bowl. The surrounding fog thickens like curdled milk as ash-caked guardians drag themselves up to be offered to the blaze.
yorgrim [angry]: Stay close within the lantern's ring and cut down whatever crawls from the ash. Spill their dust where the violet fire can watch them fall.
combat mm_violet_rite

~ violet_honor
if not flag.mm_violet_began
set mm_violet_began
set mm_violet_round = 0
set mm_violet_succ = 0
set mm_violet_bright = 0
endif
-> violet_rite

~ violet_rite
if flag.mm_violet_succ >= 6
-> violet_done
endif
if flag.mm_yorgrim_spent and flag.mm_violet_succ >= 4
-> violet_done
endif
if flag.mm_violet_round >= 10
-> violet_dies
endif
Narrator: The violet blaze leans toward your voices, hungry for true remembrance of her healing hands, her devotion to Marius, or the hymns of her owl-winged goddess.
* Speak of the cures she made -> violet_a
* Write the letter she never sent -> violet_b
* Sing the Nightmother's hymn -> violet_c
* Step back from the flame for now -> END


~ violet_a
if flag.mem_lethica_healing
advantage checks next: you remember Lethica
endif
Narrator: You turn the rite toward the fevers she cooled and the pilgrims who knelt at her door. Each of you searches for the clearest memory of her mercy.
* [Medicine DC 15] Speak of the cures she made, the way you have heard it -> violet_a_ok | violet_a_miss
* [Nature DC 15] Speak of the cures she made, another way -> violet_a_ok | violet_a_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> violet_a_ok | violet_a_miss
* Choose another theme -> violet_rite

~ violet_a_ok
set mm_violet_succ += 1
set mm_violet_round += 1
if flag.mem_lethica_healing
set mm_violet_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The violet flame surges upward, shedding a warm scent of crushed lavender and clean linen across the damp stones. Your words land true, honoring the gentle hands that mended so many broken strangers.
-> violet_rite

~ violet_a_miss
set mm_violet_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: Your words fall flat, and the shrouded dead twist the violet fire into a masked leech poisoning a begging child. Every person in the circle flinches from the shrill, cackling chorus that echoes through the gardens.
-> violet_rite


~ violet_b
if flag.mem_lethica_love
advantage checks next: you remember Lethica
endif
Narrator: You turn your voices toward the masked woman who laid her armor down for a wrathful knight. Each hero reaches for words that honor the love she bore for Marius.
* [Investigation DC 15] Write the letter she never sent, the way you have heard it -> violet_b_ok | violet_b_miss
* [History DC 15] Write the letter she never sent, another way -> violet_b_ok | violet_b_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> violet_b_ok | violet_b_miss
* Choose another theme -> violet_rite

~ violet_b_ok
set mm_violet_succ += 1
set mm_violet_round += 1
if flag.mem_lethica_love
set mm_violet_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The violet fire leaps high and steady, braided with a warm thread of crimson light. Your words ring true, calling back the quiet touch that tamed a warrior's rage.
-> violet_rite

~ violet_b_miss
set mm_violet_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: The tribute misses its mark, and spiteful spirits bend the flame into two lovers tearing at each other's throats behind iron masks. A sharp chill bites your skin as the watching mist hisses with delight.
-> violet_rite


~ violet_c
if flag.mem_lethica_hymns
advantage checks next: you remember Lethica
endif
Narrator: You guide the rite toward the soft nocturnal prayers of the Nightmother and the white owl that watched over her shrine. Each of you reaches for the cadence of her old hymns.
* [Religion DC 15] Sing the Nightmother's hymn, the way you have heard it -> violet_c_ok | violet_c_miss
* [Arcana DC 15] Sing the Nightmother's hymn, another way -> violet_c_ok | violet_c_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> violet_c_ok | violet_c_miss
* Choose another theme -> violet_rite

~ violet_c_ok
set mm_violet_succ += 1
set mm_violet_round += 1
if flag.mem_lethica_hymns
set mm_violet_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The violet flame leaps high as your spoken melody rings true, carrying the old vespers of the Nightmother across the cold ash. Soft owl-feather shadows rise in the heat, warming the stone beneath your boots.
-> violet_rite

~ violet_c_miss
set mm_violet_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: Your words stumble, and the shrouded dead twist the Nightmother's hymn into a screeching choir of strangled birds inside the fire. Everyone in the lantern ring flinches back from that sour, ringing discord.
-> violet_rite


~ violet_dies
Narrator: The last grain of time runs out, and the violet flame gutters down into cold black grease. Yorgrim reaches a grey hand into his own chest, tearing loose a pale blue spark to keep the ember alive.
set mm_soul_fragments += 1
set mm_rite_fails += 1
disadvantage checks 1h: a piece of your soul is in the fire
set mm_violet_round = 0
set mm_violet_succ = 0
set mm_violet_bright = 0
if flag.mm_rite_fails >= 2
set mm_yorgrim_spent
yorgrim [weary]: I will feed more of my own marrow into the ash so the fire asks fewer words of you next time. My hands look thinner in the lantern light now, but the work remains.
else
yorgrim [neutral]: The ember still holds its heat, so draw your breath and try the words again without blame.
endif
-> END

~ violet_done
set beacon_violet = 1
if flag.mm_violet_bright >= 3
set beacon_violet = 2
endif
if flag.mm_violet_bright >= 6
set beacon_violet = 3
endif
set mm_beacons_lit += 1
set mm_violet_done
cutscene mm_beacon_lit
Narrator: The violet beacon roars up like a furnace, driving the clammy shroud back from the bone-white urns of the Cremation Gardens. Far across the cemetery, a solitary sconce catches fire above the great sepulcher doors.
yorgrim [smile]: Lethica walks under quiet feathers once more, gentle as the dusk she kept. You gave her back her true name before the dark took her.
if flag.mm_beacons_lit >= 5
set sepulcher_open
if not quest.maidenmist_dead_rise >= sepulcher
quest maidenmist_dead_rise sepulcher
endif
yorgrim [weary]: Five fires burn against the gray, and my own blue lantern grows light in the chain. The heavy sepulcher doors will unbar for us now, so come back to the center.
endif
-> END


~ amber_start
if flag.mm_amber_guardians_dead
-> amber_honor
endif
Narrator: You stand before a rusted iron brazier in the sunken mud of the Potter's Field, where crooked wooden markers rot in the wet clay. Isolde holds her hooded lantern steady in her jaws, pressing the grave-mist back a few paces.
yorgrim [weary]: Jericho was a scarecrow man with a battered banjo, walking the muddy roads to trade songs for supper. Children followed his dry straw coat through every village, and he listened to their small troubles as hard as he played. He mended broken plows, split kindling, and left every leaning fence straighter than he found it.
* [if item:mm_straw_bundle] Place the kindling in the brazier -> amber_kindle
* I have no kindling yet -> amber_nokindle
* Tell us again what you know of Jericho -> amber_start
* We will be back -> END

~ amber_nokindle
yorgrim [neutral]: The dry straw for his fire is tucked under some stone nearby, though the fog has eaten where I laid it. Look again among the markers, nothing is lost yet.
-> END

~ amber_kindle
take mm_straw_bundle
set mm_amber_kindled
Narrator: The dry straw catches in the iron bowl, and a warm amber fire climbs with the smell of autumn harvest. Beyond the light, the wet clay churns as restless dead claw free to throw themselves at the blaze.
yorgrim [angry]: Keep your boots inside the lantern ring and cut down whatever crawls from the mud. Their husks must fall where the amber fire can see them die.
combat mm_amber_rite

~ amber_honor
if not flag.mm_amber_began
set mm_amber_began
set mm_amber_round = 0
set mm_amber_succ = 0
set mm_amber_bright = 0
endif
-> amber_rite

~ amber_rite
if flag.mm_amber_succ >= 6
-> amber_done
endif
if flag.mm_yorgrim_spent and flag.mm_amber_succ >= 4
-> amber_done
endif
if flag.mm_amber_round >= 10
-> amber_dies
endif
Narrator: The amber flame leans toward your breath, hungry for the honest measure of Ol' Jericho Sticks in the songs he strummed, the tall tales he spun, and the humble work of his straw-stuffed hands.
* Play one of his songs -> amber_a
* Tell one of his tall tales -> amber_b
* Speak of the work of his hands -> amber_c
* Step back from the flame for now -> END


~ amber_a
if flag.mem_jericho_songs
advantage checks next: you remember Jericho
endif
Narrator: You turn the rite toward the porch-step tunes Jericho plucked on his old gut-string banjo. Each of you searches your memory for a chorus warm enough to beat back the damp.
* [Sleight of Hand DC 15] Play one of his songs, the way you have heard it -> amber_a_ok | amber_a_miss
* [History DC 15] Play one of his songs, another way -> amber_a_ok | amber_a_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> amber_a_ok | amber_a_miss
* Choose another theme -> amber_rite

~ amber_a_ok
set mm_amber_succ += 1
set mm_amber_round += 1
if flag.mem_jericho_songs
set mm_amber_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The amber fire surges up with a crackle like dry pine, humming with the steady rhythm of a country reel. For a breath, the sour mud smells of cider and rosin.
-> amber_rite

~ amber_a_miss
set mm_amber_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: The cadence breaks on your tongue, and the shrouded spirits in the smoke rasp back a broken, snapping-string mockery of Jericho's tune. You wince as the sour noise scrapes across your teeth.
-> amber_rite


~ amber_b
if flag.mem_jericho_tales
advantage checks next: you remember Jericho
endif
Narrator: You steer the words toward the cheerful whoppers Jericho told around village hearths to make frightened folk laugh. Each of you reaches for the wildest yarn that still rings true.
* [Investigation DC 15] Tell one of his tall tales, the way you have heard it -> amber_b_ok | amber_b_miss
* [History DC 15] Tell one of his tall tales, another way -> amber_b_ok | amber_b_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> amber_b_ok | amber_b_miss
* Choose another theme -> amber_rite

~ amber_b_ok
set mm_amber_succ += 1
set mm_amber_round += 1
if flag.mem_jericho_tales
set mm_amber_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The flame jumps bright and golden, dancing like grease in a hot skillet as the tall tale lands right. A dry, rustling chuckle seems to pass through the dead weeds at your ankles.
-> amber_rite

~ amber_b_miss
set mm_amber_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: The story sours in the telling, and the hungry shapes in the fire twist the yarn into a spiteful lie about rotting harvests and starved children. The cruel hiss of it makes every shoulder round against the cold.
-> amber_rite


~ amber_c
if flag.mem_jericho_craft
advantage checks next: you remember Jericho
endif
Narrator: You bring the rite home to the calloused work of his hands, mending tools and turning stubborn soil for strangers. Each of you names a quiet kindness left behind in barn or field.
* [Survival DC 15] Speak of the work of his hands, the way you have heard it -> amber_c_ok | amber_c_miss
* [Nature DC 15] Speak of the work of his hands, another way -> amber_c_ok | amber_c_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> amber_c_ok | amber_c_miss
* Choose another theme -> amber_rite

~ amber_c_ok
set mm_amber_succ += 1
set mm_amber_round += 1
if flag.mem_jericho_craft
set mm_amber_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The amber blaze swells thick and steady, throwing out the honest heat of a blacksmith's forge and freshly turned earth. The frost on the iron brazier melts away in a hiss of steam.
-> amber_rite

~ amber_c_miss
set mm_amber_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: Your words miss the mark, and the shrouded dead curl the smoke into the shape of a broken pitchfork and a burning barn. The bitter stink of charred burlap makes you turn your faces aside.
-> amber_rite


~ amber_dies
Narrator: The minute bleeds away, and the golden flame sinks down into a sullen smudge of black soot. Yorgrim bows his chained shoulders and breaks off another pale splinter of his own spirit to shelter the spark.
set mm_soul_fragments += 1
set mm_rite_fails += 1
disadvantage checks 1h: a piece of your soul is in the fire
set mm_amber_round = 0
set mm_amber_succ = 0
set mm_amber_bright = 0
if flag.mm_rite_fails >= 2
set mm_yorgrim_spent
yorgrim [weary]: Take another piece of my breath to grease the wood, and the fire will not ask so much of your voices. The names carved on my back feel heavier when I fade like this.
else
yorgrim [neutral]: No fault lies on your tongues, and the spark still waits in the straw whenever you are ready to speak.
endif
-> END

~ amber_done
set beacon_amber = 1
if flag.mm_amber_bright >= 3
set beacon_amber = 2
endif
if flag.mm_amber_bright >= 6
set beacon_amber = 3
endif
set mm_beacons_lit += 1
set mm_amber_done
cutscene mm_beacon_lit
Narrator: The amber beacon roars high, rolling the cold fog back from the sunken trenches of the Potter's Field like dry chaff before a broom. Far away through the iron palings, another sconce flares to life above the sepulcher doors.
yorgrim [smile]: Old straw and sweet music, that was the whole of him before the rot set in. He rests easy in the dark now because you remembered.
if flag.mm_beacons_lit >= 5
set sepulcher_open
if not quest.maidenmist_dead_rise >= sepulcher
quest maidenmist_dead_rise sepulcher
endif
yorgrim [weary]: All five beacons answer my blue lantern now, and the weight on my chains is nearly done. The sepulcher doors are unsealed, so walk with me back to the middle.
endif
-> END


~ magenta_start
if flag.mm_magenta_guardians_dead
-> magenta_honor
endif
Narrator: You stand between the towering marble vaults of the Mausoleum Lanes, where cold rainwater drips from carved gargoyles into a dark bronze brazier. Isolde's lantern casts long, sharp shadows across the wet flagstones, holding the gray shroud at bay.
yorgrim [weary]: Briggsy Kratch was a cutthroat pirate with a soft heart, who never once left a loyal sailor behind on the gallows. He fought with a fast blade and a faster tongue, smiling through every trap he laid. Luck loved him at cards and dice until he grew greedy and bound fate itself with crooked sorcery.
* [if item:mm_rum_bottle] Place the kindling in the brazier -> magenta_kindle
* I have no kindling yet -> magenta_nokindle
* Tell us again what you know of Briggsy -> magenta_start
* We will be back -> END

~ magenta_nokindle
yorgrim [neutral]: The salt-tarred wood for his brazier is stashed in one of these stone niches, though my head is too thick with mist to name which. Search the crypts again, the dead have nothing better to do than wait.
-> END

~ magenta_kindle
take mm_rum_bottle
set mm_magenta_kindled
Narrator: The tarred kindling catches with a hiss of salt spray, sending a fierce magenta flame twisting toward the marble roofs. Out in the lanes, rusted crypt gates shriek open as armored bones march forth to feed the fire.
yorgrim [angry]: Stand fast within the lantern's circle and break the bones that cross the flagstones. Spill them where the magenta fire can drink their shadow.
combat mm_magenta_rite

~ magenta_honor
if not flag.mm_magenta_began
set mm_magenta_began
set mm_magenta_round = 0
set mm_magenta_succ = 0
set mm_magenta_bright = 0
endif
-> magenta_rite

~ magenta_rite
if flag.mm_magenta_succ >= 6
-> magenta_done
endif
if flag.mm_yorgrim_spent and flag.mm_magenta_succ >= 4
-> magenta_done
endif
if flag.mm_magenta_round >= 10
-> magenta_dies
endif
Narrator: The hungry magenta ember waits on your breath, asking whether you will recall the Captain's salt-stained voyages, his nimble blade and cunning tricks, or the charmed dice that carried him through the storm.
* Tell of his voyages -> magenta_a
* Speak of his ruses and his swordwork -> magenta_b
* Speak of his luck at the tables -> magenta_c
* Step back from the flame for now -> END


~ magenta_a
if flag.mem_briggsy_exploits
advantage checks next: you remember Briggsy
endif
Narrator: You turn your thoughts toward the open sea and the creak of wet rigging. Each of you searches for the true measure of the sailor behind the tall tales.
* [History DC 15] Tell of his voyages, the way you have heard it -> magenta_a_ok | magenta_a_miss
* [Survival DC 15] Tell of his voyages, another way -> magenta_a_ok | magenta_a_miss
* [Charisma DC 18] Offer a memory of your own -> magenta_a_ok | magenta_a_miss
* Choose another theme -> magenta_rite

~ magenta_a_ok
set mm_magenta_succ += 1
set mm_magenta_round += 1
if flag.mem_briggsy_exploits
set mm_magenta_bright += 1
endif
Narrator: The magenta fire leaps high with the sudden smell of brine and tar, warming to the truth of a captain who steered through black squalls for his crew.
-> magenta_rite

~ magenta_a_miss
set mm_magenta_round += 1
damage 1d6 psychic party
Narrator: Your words ring hollow against the cold iron, and the shrouded twist the smoke into a drowning hull choked with bilge and broken oars. A wet, mocking rattle rises from the brazier, and every soul around the fire flinches from the sound.
-> magenta_rite


~ magenta_b
if flag.mem_briggsy_ruses
advantage checks next: you remember Briggsy
